    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Studying how other nations achieved rapid economic transformation offers valuable <span class=\"learn-keyword\">development lessons</span> for Nigeria. This topic examines the economic history of the \"Asian Tigers,\" Japan, and other developed economies between 1960 and 2000.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Who Are the \"Asian Tigers\"?</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Asian Tigers</span> refers to four East Asian economies — South Korea, Taiwan, Hong Kong, and Singapore — that experienced extraordinarily rapid industrialisation and economic growth between the 1960s and 1990s, transforming from largely agrarian economies into major industrial and financial powers.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Japan's Post-War Economic Miracle</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">After the devastation of World War II, Japan achieved rapid economic recovery and growth from the 1950s through the 1980s, becoming one of the world's largest economies. This transformation is often called the \"Japanese economic miracle.\"</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Key Factors Behind These Economies' Success</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Export-oriented industrialisation</td><td>Focusing production on goods for export to earn foreign exchange and drive growth</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Heavy investment in education</td><td>Building a skilled, literate workforce capable of adopting new technologies</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Strong government planning</td><td>Coordinated national development plans directing resources toward strategic industries</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>High savings and investment rates</td><td>Citizens and businesses saved heavily, providing capital for industrial investment</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Technology transfer and adaptation</td><td>Learning from and improving upon technologies developed elsewhere</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Europe and America's Development Path</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Western European nations and the United States achieved development through earlier industrialisation (from the 18th and 19th centuries), building strong institutions, property rights, technological innovation, and gradually expanding trade and financial systems over a longer historical period than the Asian Tigers.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember the four Asian Tiger economies specifically: South Korea, Taiwan, Hong Kong, and Singapore. WAEC frequently asks candidates to name them correctly.\n</div>\n",
