    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Building on the historical overview, this topic reviews the specific <span class=\"learn-keyword\">development strategies</span> employed by these successful economies and draws direct lessons applicable to the Nigerian economy.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Review of Development Strategies</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Strategy</th><th>How It Was Applied</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Import substitution (early stage)</td><td>Initially producing goods locally to replace imports, protecting infant industries</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Shift to export promotion</td><td>Once industries matured, shifting focus to competing in export markets</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Infrastructure investment</td><td>Heavy government spending on roads, ports, electricity, and telecommunications</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Political and macroeconomic stability</td><td>Maintaining stable governments and controlled inflation, attracting investor confidence</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Foreign direct investment (FDI) attraction</td><td>Creating favourable conditions to attract capital and expertise from foreign investors</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Key Lessons for the Nigerian Economy</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Diversify away from oil dependency:</strong> Like the Asian Tigers diversified beyond agriculture, Nigeria should reduce reliance on oil revenue by developing manufacturing and other export sectors</li>\n  <li><strong>Invest in human capital:</strong> Prioritise education and skills training to build a competitive workforce</li>\n  <li><strong>Improve infrastructure:</strong> Reliable power, transportation, and communication are essential foundations for industrial growth</li>\n  <li><strong>Ensure political and economic stability:</strong> Consistent policies and low corruption attract both domestic and foreign investment</li>\n  <li><strong>Encourage savings and local investment:</strong> Policies that promote domestic saving and channel it into productive investment</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Challenges in Applying These Lessons to Nigeria</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Nigeria faces distinct challenges compared to the Asian Tigers, including a much larger and more diverse population, significant infrastructure deficits, governance and corruption issues, and a different starting point in global trade competitiveness — meaning strategies must be adapted, not simply copied.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> When answering essay questions on \"lessons for Nigeria,\" always link each lesson explicitly back to a specific Nigerian economic challenge (e.g., oil dependency, unemployment, infrastructure deficit) rather than stating the lesson generically.\n</div>\n",
