    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Manufacturing</span> and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">construction</span> are key sectors of the secondary industry, transforming raw materials into finished goods and building the physical infrastructure that supports all other economic activities.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning and Types of Manufacturing</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Manufacturing</span> is the process of converting raw materials into finished or semi-finished goods through the application of labour, machinery, and processes.</p>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Craft/artisanal manufacturing</td><td>Small-scale, often hand-made production, e.g., pottery, weaving</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Food processing</td><td>Converting raw agricultural produce into packaged food products, e.g., flour milling, canning</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Heavy manufacturing</td><td>Large-scale industrial production, e.g., steel, cement, automobiles</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Light manufacturing</td><td>Smaller-scale production of consumer goods, e.g., textiles, furniture</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Meaning of Construction</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Construction</span> refers to the process of building and assembling infrastructure, such as roads, bridges, buildings, and dams — a distinct but related secondary sector activity.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Contributions to Nigeria's GDP</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Manufacturing and construction contribute to Nigeria's Gross Domestic Product (GDP) by adding value to raw materials, generating employment, and creating physical assets (buildings, roads) that support further economic activity across all sectors.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Roles in Economic Development</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Creating employment opportunities across skilled and unskilled labour categories</li>\n  <li>Adding value to raw materials, increasing their economic worth before sale or export</li>\n  <li>Supporting urbanisation and infrastructure development through construction activities</li>\n  <li>Encouraging technology adoption and skills transfer within the workforce</li>\n  <li>Reducing dependence on imported finished goods by producing them domestically</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Don't confuse manufacturing (transforming raw materials into goods) with construction (building physical infrastructure) — though both are secondary sector activities, WAEC tests the distinction between what each actually produces.\n</div>\n",
