    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Services</span> form the tertiary sector of the economy — intangible activities that support and facilitate all other economic sectors, rather than producing physical goods directly.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Services</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Services</span> are intangible economic activities that satisfy needs and wants without producing a physical, tangible product — for example, transporting people, providing financial advice, or offering insurance protection.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Types of Service Industries</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Service Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Tourism</td><td>Services related to travel, hospitality, and leisure activities for visitors</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Transport</td><td>Moving people and goods from one location to another (road, rail, air, water)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Banking</td><td>Financial services including savings, loans, and payment processing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Providing financial protection against risk in exchange for premium payments</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Warehousing</td><td>Storage of goods before distribution or sale</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Advertisement</td><td>Promoting goods and services to potential customers</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Contributions of Service Industries to National Development</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Generating employment across a wide range of skill levels</li>\n  <li>Supporting trade and commerce by enabling transportation, storage, and marketing of goods</li>\n  <li>Providing financial infrastructure (banking, insurance) that supports investment and risk management</li>\n  <li>Attracting foreign exchange, particularly through tourism</li>\n  <li>Facilitating the flow of information and connecting buyers with sellers through advertisement</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Why Services Matter for a Modern Economy</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">As economies develop, the service sector typically grows to become the largest contributor to GDP, since services support and enable activity across agriculture, manufacturing, and trade — without efficient transport, banking, and insurance, other productive sectors would struggle to function effectively.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember that services are \"intangible\" — you cannot physically touch or store a service itself (unlike goods), even though the activity may support the storage or movement of physical goods.\n</div>\n",
