    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Financial markets require careful <span class=\"learn-keyword\">regulation</span> to protect investors, maintain stability, and ensure fair practices. Nigeria has distinct regulatory bodies for its money market (short-term funds) and capital market (long-term investments).\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Regulation of the Money Market</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">money market</span> deals with short-term borrowing and lending (typically under one year), such as treasury bills and commercial paper.</p>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Agency</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Central Bank of Nigeria (CBN)</td><td>Regulates commercial banks, sets monetary policy, controls interest rates, and issues currency</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC)</td><td>Insures bank deposits, protecting depositors if a bank fails</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Regulation of the Capital Market</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">capital market</span> deals with long-term investments, such as shares and bonds.</p>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Agency</th><th>Objectives and Tools</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC)</td><td>Objective: protect investors and ensure fair, transparent trading. Tools: registration requirements, disclosure rules, monitoring of market operators</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Nigerian Exchange Group (NGX)</td><td>Objective: provide an organised marketplace for trading shares and bonds. Tools: listing requirements, trading rules, price monitoring</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Functions and Significance of Regulatory Agencies</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Protecting investors and depositors from fraud and financial instability</li>\n  <li>Maintaining confidence in the financial system, encouraging savings and investment</li>\n  <li>Ensuring fair and transparent trading practices in financial markets</li>\n  <li>Supporting monetary policy implementation to control inflation and manage the money supply</li>\n  <li>Preventing systemic financial crises through oversight and early intervention</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember: CBN and NDIC regulate the MONEY market (short-term); SEC and the Nigerian Exchange Group regulate the CAPITAL market (long-term). WAEC often tests which agency belongs to which market.\n</div>\n",
