    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Building on the fundamentals of international trade, this topic examines <span class=\"learn-keyword\">globalization</span> — the increasing interconnectedness of the world's economies — and what it means for Nigeria.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Globalization</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Globalization</span> is the process by which economies, societies, and cultures around the world become increasingly interconnected through trade, investment, technology, and the flow of information, capital, and people across borders.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Features of Globalization</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Rapid growth in international trade and cross-border investment</li>\n  <li>Advances in communication technology (internet, mobile phones) connecting people worldwide instantly</li>\n  <li>The rise of multinational corporations operating across many countries</li>\n  <li>Increased movement of capital, labour, and ideas across national borders</li>\n  <li>Greater cultural exchange and interconnectedness between nations</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Challenges of Globalization</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Increased competition can threaten local industries unable to compete with efficient foreign producers</li>\n  <li>Risk of job losses in sectors that cannot compete internationally</li>\n  <li>Growing inequality between those who benefit from global integration and those left behind</li>\n  <li>Loss of cultural identity as global (often Western) culture spreads</li>\n  <li>Increased vulnerability to global economic shocks (e.g., a financial crisis in one region spreading worldwide)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Opportunities Globalization Presents to the Nigerian Economy</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Access to larger export markets for Nigerian goods and services</li>\n  <li>Potential for increased foreign direct investment (FDI) inflows</li>\n  <li>Access to new technologies and knowledge transfer from developed economies</li>\n  <li>Opportunities for Nigerian entrepreneurs to participate in global value chains</li>\n  <li>Greater access to international capital markets for financing development</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> When discussing globalization in an essay, always balance the discussion — present BOTH the challenges AND the opportunities it presents for Nigeria, since WAEC frequently asks for both sides.\n</div>\n",
