    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Economic development planning</span> is the deliberate process by which a government sets goals and coordinates resources to achieve specific economic and social objectives over a defined period.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Economic Planning</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><span class=\"learn-keyword\">Economic planning</span> is a deliberate government effort to influence, direct, or control economic activities to achieve set targets, such as growth rates, employment levels, or infrastructure development, within a specified timeframe.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Types of Economic Plans by Duration</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Duration</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Short-term plan</td><td>1–2 years</td><td>Addresses immediate, urgent economic issues</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Medium-term plan</td><td>3–5 years</td><td>Sets intermediate development goals and strategies</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Long-term (perspective) plan</td><td>10–25 years or more</td><td>Sets a broad, overarching vision for national development</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Objectives of Economic Planning</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Achieving sustained economic growth</li>\n  <li>Reducing unemployment and underemployment</li>\n  <li>Reducing poverty and income inequality</li>\n  <li>Improving infrastructure and industrial capacity</li>\n  <li>Achieving balanced regional development across the country</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Stages of the Planning Process</h3>\n<ol class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Assessment of current economic conditions and available resources</li>\n  <li>Setting clear, measurable development goals and targets</li>\n  <li>Formulation of specific policies and strategies to achieve the goals</li>\n  <li>Implementation of the plan, allocating budgets and resources accordingly</li>\n  <li>Monitoring and evaluation to track progress and make necessary adjustments</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">5. Problems of Economic Planning in Nigeria</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Inadequate and unreliable statistical data for accurate planning</li>\n  <li>Political instability disrupting the continuity of long-term plans</li>\n  <li>Corruption and mismanagement of allocated resources</li>\n  <li>Over-reliance on oil revenue, making plans vulnerable to price shocks</li>\n  <li>Weak implementation and monitoring capacity within government institutions</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> A well-designed plan can still fail due to poor implementation — always distinguish between problems in the PLANNING stage (poor data, unclear goals) and problems in the IMPLEMENTATION stage (corruption, political instability) in your answers.\n</div>\n",
