    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Various <span class=\"learn-keyword\">international economic organizations</span> exist to promote cooperation, stability, and development among member nations, with Nigeria participating actively in several.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Key International Economic Organizations</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Organization</th><th>Main Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>International Monetary Fund (IMF)</td><td>Promotes global monetary cooperation, exchange rate stability, and provides financial assistance to member countries facing balance of payments problems</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>World Bank</td><td>Provides loans and grants to developing countries for development projects, such as infrastructure, education, and health</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>World Trade Organization (WTO)</td><td>Sets and enforces rules for international trade, resolving trade disputes between member nations</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>African Development Bank (AfDB)</td><td>Provides financing and technical assistance specifically to African countries for development projects</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Economic Community of West African States (ECOWAS)</td><td>Promotes regional economic integration and cooperation among West African nations</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA)</td><td>Aims to create a single market for goods and services across African countries, reducing trade barriers</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Nigeria's Membership and Participation</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Nigeria is an active member of all these organizations, participating in their programmes, accessing financial and technical assistance, and engaging in regional and global trade agreements to support its own economic development.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Benefits of Membership to Nigeria</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Access to development financing (loans, grants) for infrastructure and social projects</li>\n  <li>Technical assistance and expertise in economic policy-making</li>\n  <li>Access to wider regional and global markets through reduced trade barriers</li>\n  <li>A platform to participate in setting international trade and economic rules</li>\n  <li>Support during economic crises, such as balance of payments difficulties</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Challenges of Membership</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Loans often come with conditions (conditionalities) that may require difficult domestic policy reforms</li>\n  <li>Increased exposure to global economic competition, which can challenge weaker domestic industries</li>\n  <li>Obligations to comply with international trade rules that may sometimes conflict with domestic priorities</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Don't confuse the IMF (focused on monetary/financial stability, short-term balance of payments support) with the World Bank (focused on long-term development project financing) — WAEC frequently tests this distinction.\n</div>\n",
